From 0b820e1fdb6661373c71f49a12880562d9783544 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:58:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] debug(allwinner): PM event trace page and runtime
 experiment knob

Bring-up aid only, not for upstream. The Allwinner BL31 console has no
runtime scope and printing from PSCI handlers after the OS has gated the
UART clock would hang BL31, so record PM events in the last page of the
BL31 DRAM reservation instead (SUNXI_PM_TRACE_BASE = 0x4003f000, mapped
non-cacheable, a system ring plus one lock-free ring per core, survives
warm resets; the per-core rings freeze after a warm reset until the OS
re-arms them) where the OS (/dev/mem) or U-Boot (md.l) can read them.
The same page carries a knob, reset to 0 at every boot, that selects
cpu-sleep experiments at runtime (WFI only / the regular sequence with
or without the GIC CPU interface / either with core 0 never gated) and
lets the system suspend path skip the DRAM self-refresh, the CPU clock
change or the SRAM relocation. Modes whose WFI may return restart the
core through the warm boot entry point instead of letting the generic
code panic.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
